  "text": "The magnitude of the complex numbers found in part \n5\n equals \n4√15 .\n\tCorrect\nExplanation\n\nLet's pick the complex number \n𝑧\n=\n−\n8\n+\n4\n11\ni\n.\n\nFor a complex number \n𝑧\n=\n𝑎\n+\n𝑏\ni\n,\n the magnitude of \n𝑧\n is given by\n|\n𝑧\n|\n=\n𝑎\n2\n+\n𝑏\n2\n.\n\nFor the complex number \n𝑧\n=\n−\n8\n+\n4\n11\ni\n,\n we have \n𝑎\n=\n−\n8\n and \n𝑏\n=\n4\n11\n.\n So, the magnitude is given by\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\n|\n−\n8\n+\n4\n11\ni\n|\n\t\n=\n(\n−\n8\n)\n2\n+\n(\n4\n11\n)\n2\n\n\t\n=\n8\n2\n+\n4\n2\n⋅\n11\n\n\t\n=\n4\n2\n⋅\n2\n2\n+\n4\n2\n⋅\n11\n\n\t\n=\n4\n2\n⋅\n(\n4\n+\n11\n)\n\n\t\n=\n4\n15\n."
